WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.722
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:09.780
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:17.864
Unit one: Studying in English at University. Today you will understand what academic English is and how university study works.

4
00:00:18.164 --> 00:00:20.886
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:25.020
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.792
Lecture.

7
00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:30.549
Lecture means a talk given to many students.

8
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.813
The lecture starts at nine.

9
00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:35.790
Your turn. Say: Lecture.

10
00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:39.658
Lecture.

11
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:41.464
Seminar.

12
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.100
Seminar means a small discussion class.

13
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:47.962
We discuss ideas in a seminar.

14
00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.947
Your turn. Say: Seminar.

15
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.813
Seminar.

16
00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:56.551
Assignment.

17
00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.654
Assignment means a piece of set work.

18
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.191
Finish the assignment by Friday.

19
00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:05.203
Your turn. Say: Assignment.

20
00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.021
Assignment.

21
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:10.680
Deadline.

22
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:14.031
Deadline means the last date to finish.

23
00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:16.372
The deadline is next week.

24
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:19.740
Your turn. Say: Deadline.

25
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.497
Deadline.

26
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.065
Tutor.

27
00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.572
Tutor means a teacher who guides a student.

28
00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:30.939
My tutor read my essay.

29
00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.912
Your turn. Say: Tutor.

30
00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:37.524
Tutor.

31
00:01:38.283 --> 00:01:39.284
Module.

32
00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:42.689
Module means one part of a degree course.

33
00:01:43.283 --> 00:01:45.086
I chose a business module.

34
00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:48.243
Your turn. Say: Module.

35
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.089
Module.

36
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:53.956
Independent.

37
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:57.298
Independent means working without much help.

38
00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.384
Be an independent learner.

39
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:02.787
Your turn. Say: Independent.

40
00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:06.681
Independent.

41
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:08.429
Academic.

42
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:12.554
Academic means connected with study and education.

43
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.057
Academic writing is formal.

44
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.349
Your turn. Say: Academic.

45
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.178
Academic.

46
00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:26.722
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:30.628
Visal, what is different about studying at university?

48
00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:41.022
You attend lectures and seminars, read many texts and write long assignments. Students must be independent and manage their own time.

49
00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:43.907
What is academic English?

50
00:02:45.017 --> 00:02:54.089
It is the formal English used in books, lectures and essays. It is clear, careful and based on evidence, not on opinion alone.

51
00:02:55.183 --> 00:02:56.637
How can I prepare?

52
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:09.493
Read academic texts every week, learn key vocabulary, practise note-taking and ask your tutor when you do not understand. Good habits start early.

53
00:03:10.633 --> 00:03:12.145
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.983 --> 00:03:16.759
Grammar focus: Present simple for routines and facts.

55
00:03:17.059 --> 00:03:18.269
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.983 --> 00:03:21.227
Students attend lectures every week.

57
00:03:22.117 --> 00:03:24.163
A tutor gives advice on essays.

58
00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:32.002
Use the present simple for routines and general facts. Add s to the verb after he, she, it and singular nouns.

59
00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.830
Be careful! Don't say: A tutor give advice on essays.

60
00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:41.753
Say: A tutor gives advice on essays.

61
00:03:42.053 --> 00:03:44.145
Add s after a singular noun.

62
00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:47.725
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:49.813
My First Week.

64
00:03:50.113 --> 00:03:52.705
Dara starts university in September.

65
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.768
He attends two lectures and one seminar each day.

66
00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.242
His tutor gives him a long reading list.

67
00:04:01.233 --> 00:04:03.709
Dara must manage his own time carefully.

68
00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.967
He writes every deadline in his planner.

69
00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:11.859
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:12.717 --> 00:04:15.250
A seminar is a small blank class.

71
00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:19.343
A, cooking. B, discussion. C, sports.

72
00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.923
The answer is B: discussion.

73
00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:28.292
A deadline is the last blank to finish.

74
00:04:28.592 --> 00:04:31.816
A, book. B, room. C, date.

75
00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.006
The answer is C: date.

76
00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.161
A tutor blank students.

77
00:04:40.461 --> 00:04:44.173
A, guides. B, avoids. C, forgets.

78
00:04:47.733 --> 00:04:49.721
The answer is A: guides.

79
00:04:50.883 --> 00:04:53.533
An independent learner works with little blank.

80
00:04:53.833 --> 00:04:57.196
A, noise. B, help. C, energy.

81
00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.454
The answer is B: help.

82
00:05:03.617 --> 00:05:05.605
Where does Dara write deadlines?

83
00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:09.593
A, on a wall. B, on a bus. C, in a planner.

84
00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:15.423
The answer is C: in a planner.

85
00:05:16.633 --> 00:05:20.029
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.883 --> 00:05:23.231
What is different about university study?

87
00:05:32.017 --> 00:05:33.540
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:45.772
At university I study more independently. I attend lectures and seminars, read many texts and write long assignments. I must manage my time and meet every deadline.

89
00:05:46.072 --> 00:05:47.862
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:54.038
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present simple for routines and facts.

91
00:05:54.338 --> 00:05:59.173
Today's value is independence. Learn to do things by yourself, step by step.

92
00:05:59.473 --> 00:06:01.649
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

93
00:06:01.949 --> 00:06:05.043
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

